from his theories on the antichrist and AI to his distinctive politics, Peter Thiel is hard to pin down.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia: Ukrainian drone strike on Moscow kills 2</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f76a30ef9714e1aa71170e74ceb290c55173007373c486b8cb1ddc171087d5d</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T08:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-ukrainian-drone-strike-on-moscow-kills-2/a-79341964--f3da33d772e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-ukrainian-drone-strike-on-moscow-kills-2/a-79341964?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An oil refinery was hit in one of the largest attacks so far on the Russian capital, as the country holds a parliamentary election. Meanwhile, at least four people were killed in Russian strikes in Ukraine's Kyiv region.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ed Sheeran speaks on Gaza in concert after Macklemore controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a49869568744b380cc2ccc6c15503d1c7e41169b948212b16d2609c022c840b7</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ed-sheeran-speaks-on-gaza-in-concert-after-macklemore-controversy/a-79341971--af13de157344.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ed-sheeran-speaks-on-gaza-in-concert-after-macklemore-controversy/a-79341971?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sheeran called the Hamas-led attack in Israel "horrific" and described the war in Gaza as "catastrophic and unjustifiable" during his first concert since the Macklemore controversy erupted.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>In cosmopolitan Berlin, elections still closed to foreigners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ed74ab8945055e505808507fd07420a1cd0de56855c1cd21e31729e01be3c5e</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T07:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579--2c7a3b66c58f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter of Berlin residents will have no say in the German capital's city-state election because they lack citizenship. That's the highest proportion of residents excluded from the election yet, and many are unhappy.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>India news: PM Modi says developing nations unfairly blamed for emissions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:591990160d3ecaa054eed6e771d77e335b10e8cfd15c16cfb93e895ca67151f5</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-pm-modi-says-developing-nations-unfairly-blamed-for-emissions/live-79335891--dbd6bc9f1890.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-pm-modi-says-developing-nations-unfairly-blamed-for-emissions/live-79335891?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">PM Narendra Modi has told a climate conference that developed countries emit six times more CO2 than India. Meanwhile, an IIT Bombay professor has been accused of caste abuse. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Doctors offer Oktoberfest flu jabs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a7bf61bfea25a25e9aa3c1ded3273486861ced79ab3be7e0acd6e90ce0d8c31</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-doctors-offer-oktoberfest-flu-jabs/live-79335548--b4ec07a0d158.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-doctors-offer-oktoberfest-flu-jabs/live-79335548?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest 2026 is underway but it's not just beer on offer in Munich this year; revelers can also get themselves a flu jab before heading to the tents. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Decolonizing perceptions about Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f82c954f968eb5d3570f495e570923497fde4f8978126cdc626ad9fc0f519eca</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/decolonizing-perceptions-about-africa/a-79331178--8deea6e78a06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/decolonizing-perceptions-about-africa/a-79331178?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As a UN resolution alters the standard global map to reflect the continent more accurately, initiatives to decolonize African schools and a campaign to present positive developments are changing the way Africa is seen.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz under pressure as AfD eyes second state win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1df86a4429b236458b7573c9df30485e94bfde83dd650590dd3419a0b6bfa635</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:54:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-voting-underway-in-two-key-state-elections/live-79322092--9f59fbb872c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-under-pressure-as-afd-eyes-second-state-win/live-79322092?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Exit polls have the far-right AfD leading the Social Democrats in Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania and the Left Party ahead in Berlin. Merz referred to the outcome as "a disaster". DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is it possible to replace the chancellor?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8baf976eff7145b3e5ad9cb870949704258aa7c68713a5d4aea2b31804202315</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T05:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623--5363f1668974.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz's record-low approval ratings have emboldened his opponents. There are three ways to remove a chancellor from office in Germany.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Dutch police disperse violent far-right protest in The Hague</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75f5f86a01743da8312d1765c92be1d3dcf3e8629c1dfa1acfe14c041ef5bcca</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T22:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dutch-police-disperse-violent-far-right-protest-in-the-hague/a-79340495--6f615f4c4297.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dutch-police-disperse-violent-far-right-protest-in-the-hague/a-79340495?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After violence broke out, Dutch riot police dispersed hundreds of far-right protesters in The Hague. Prime Minister Rob Jetten said that the demonstrators had chanted "abhorrent" far-right and antisemitic slogans.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Summer of 2026 broke records in Europe, and caused deaths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e52c7c73ce7c5d15143f7f1dc15e6b1c69f2004bff0d11c5323c135a6bcae097</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T19:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/summer-of-2026-broke-records-in-europe-and-caused-deaths/a-79339630--5efe97f5474b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/summer-of-2026-broke-records-in-europe-and-caused-deaths/a-79339630?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The summer of 2026 was not only the hottest on record in Europe, it also saw a record number of people die. More than 16,000 are thought to have died because of the heat in Germany alone.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Trump announces new 'AI force' amid mounting pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1f90859410e0f1b360faceaca1de943a09c4240bb285ff52bde8793e90ceee9</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T17:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-announces-new-ai-force-amid-mounting-pressure/a-79339935--91ffbee2e238.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-announces-new-ai-force-amid-mounting-pressure/a-79339935?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several voices, including from within the AI industry, have been calling for policing the fast-growing technology. Trump has once again called AI warnings "hoaxes" and vowed to "cherish, help" the industry.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German-Russian relations at freezing point</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c191a3b6a156e704764bb945571a3e5292d88140176fcc85abcb4f01efbef32a</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T16:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-russian-relations-at-freezing-point/a-79330741--08a579f047c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-russian-relations-at-freezing-point/a-79330741?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine destroyed the once-close relationship between Moscow and Berlin. Yet the far-right AfD is calling for a normalization of relations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine steps up measures to protect railways</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e91b668e3f61de742597ceac77f838e8b12082b67688c7dfef5a009743926095</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-steps-up-measures-to-protect-railways/a-79339087--356ca60a409d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-steps-up-measures-to-protect-railways/a-79339087?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russia increases its attacks on Ukraine's rail infrastructure, the Ukrainian government has called for help to replace destroyed locomotives and is making plans to keep passengers safe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW and Politico denied access to White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cdd829e6ea53ef533ea0755ee53a306a77c984e6130b6f6ce69e28de21eaba6</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cnn-ms-now-and-politico-denied-access-to-white-house/a-79339055--e53ebc96fb07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cnn-ms-now-and-politico-denied-access-to-white-house/a-79339055?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three US news outlets said their journalists were blocked from entering the White House grounds, hours after President Donald Trump announced bans on several media outlets.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania: Will economy shape the vote?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f56a8512b45a19ff0ce59a43b683ba3ae728e7fc50b92d78f0ed0876127d554</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-will-economy-shape-the-vote/a-79298904--432385452f89.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-will-economy-shape-the-vote/a-79298904?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Voters in the eastern state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania head to the polls on Sunday, with the Social Democrats and far-right AfD neck and neck. Here's a look at key economic issues that could influence the election.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia: Houthis claim strikes on Riyadh, Yanbu port</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e59ecc7f3486a71dded963313c4ccbc6a38b18d53881b24cb9bca36ecedba2b2</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T14:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-houthis-claim-strikes-on-riyadh-yanbu-port/a-79339010--2d1e9c3d2dd5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-houthis-claim-strikes-on-riyadh-yanbu-port/a-79339010?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Yemen-based Houthis said they targeted "sensitive sites" in Riyadh, hours after a blaze at a fuel depot near the Saudi capital's main airport. The Saudi-led coalition said Saudi defense downed a ballistic missile.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Drone sightings briefly shut Luxembourg airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd922a95a202533293fbd738c0093983e0c3474b694d25353865335ebf47f31d</id><updated>2026-09-20T18:53:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T13:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/drone-sightings-briefly-shut-luxembourg-airport/a-79338859--4dc7a358fc45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/drone-sightings-briefly-shut-luxembourg-airport/a-79338859?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Flights were diverted and hundreds of passengers affected after unauthorized drones appeared near Luxembourg's only international airport.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands protest Kennedy Center demolition fears</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb